WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.400
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.667
-Oh, man.
I love it, love it.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:06.000
-I appreciate this.
The last time we saw each other,

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.067
we were at
an Islanders playoff game.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.567
-Yes, we were.
-We were in the --

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.901
one of the last games in --
-At the Nassau Coliseum.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.834
-The Barn.
-The old Barn, the old Barn.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.834
-We got up -- we're up in --
-Visual aids.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.534
-Yeah, we were up
on the Jumbotron together.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:21.133
-Yes, we were.
-Here's us going crazy.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.167
-There we are.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.133
-Little --
Little to no enthusiasm.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.167
-Yeah, we went beyond crazy
trying to get the --

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.400
-That energy in that room
is just amazing.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.267
Almost as good as it is
right here tonight.

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:33.334
-You feeling that?
You're know what I'm saying?

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:35.000
It's like --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.467
When it's rockin'...
When it -- it's --

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.968
When you have a great crowd
and it's rockin',

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.067
there's no way to describe it.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:45.234
It -- it was like --
It was an amazing experience.

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.634
I just loved --
Singing the national anthem...

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:50.234
-Yes.
And everyone sang it along.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:51.467
It was just amazing.
-Everyone sang it so loud

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:54.534
that the girl singing
put the mic down.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:55.834
-She dropped the mic.
-She dropped the mic.

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.501
-Well, she came back for
"of the free."

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.400
-Yeah.
It's the best.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.968
-She didn't count on 15,000 --
-I got goose bumps.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.534
-It was amazing.
-But I hope I didn't bother you

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:04.868
too much, because I kept
talking to you the whole game

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.400
because I was so excited.
Because I didn't --

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.534
We didn't know
we were gonna go together.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:09.968
-No, no.
I didn't -- you surprised me.

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:11.734
I was there with my son.
It was awesome.

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.968
And we just, you know --
-I kept asking you --

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:16.901
-It was such an exciting time,

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.234
because the team
has just come into its own.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.667
They were having
a great playoff run.

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:23.334
They've won every -- almost
every game in the playoff run

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.334
they won,
except for this game, Jimmy.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.634
I'm not judging, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.767
I'm not judging.
But I will say one thing

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.734
about going to a hockey game
with Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.200
He stayed for every second.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.400
The ultimate enthusiastic,
optimistic --

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.767
even when I knew this game was
not going to happen for my team,

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.300
he was like, "We got this!
We got this!"

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.334
[ Laughter ]
-"Yeah, come on!

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:44.934
We gotta have faith!"
-We really had a great time.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I love the stories.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:49.033
I love your son.
Say hi to Daniel for me.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.133
-I will.
-But you were telling me stories

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:53.601
about how your dad
used to bring you there.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.267
-My mom and dad, we used to go
to those games when I was a kid.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.701
My childhood
was in that building.

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:01.200
So to get to share that with
my -- my kid, it was awesome.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.801
-But you were pointing out
seats where you used to sit.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.734
-Yeah, yeah. "I sat there
when they won the Stanley Cup.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.334
And I sat there
when they lost 12 in a row."

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:07.901
-It was the perfect person
to sit next to.

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:09.634
And I was bothered --
I was so intrigued by you,

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.234
I was like, "Wait, wait, wait.
So tell me what --

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:13.000
-"The game, it's over there."
-"Yeah, let's watch --

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.634
focus on the playoffs.
Yeah."

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.400
But you know what was great,
is they love you so much there.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.567
And I'll tell you this.
It was such a cool experience

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:22.334
because I'm -- you know when you
go to a stadium or you go to

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.534
an event and they go,
"Let's get loud,"

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:25.868
and then, "Let's get louder."
You know?

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.200
And they have the meter
on the Jumbotron?

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.167
Even louder than loudest is you.
-Yes.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:33.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.400
And they were doing,
"Wax on, playoffs,"

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.567
is what they were saying.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.634
-And when it got to the thing,
like, "Aah!"

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.200
we're all screaming,
and then it went to you.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.701
And I go, "Wait. What?
You're louder?"

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.400
and then they cut to you.
And -- And there was like --

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.334
[ Screaming ]
And people were freaking out.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:47.367
And they saw
where we were sitting.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.901
It was --
It was just an awesome --

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.334
-It was.
-I found something that is --

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.234
I don't know.
I think it's pretty rare.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.868
But this is --
NHL, the Islanders

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.801
actually made your --
you got your own hockey card.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:01.667
Look at this.
This is -- the Islanders made --

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:04.767
This is it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:08.567
-That was -- That was around --
That was like 1991.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:10.634
And "My Cousin Vinny"
had just come out at that time.

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:13.267
And they were -- the NHL --
it was the 75th year

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:14.667
of the National Hockey League,

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.367
so they were
going to different teams,

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:19.400
find celebrity captains,
and I got -- you know, that's --

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.701
I mean, I got a hockey card.
I mean, who else?

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.634
It was, like,
John Goodman with St. Louis.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.968
-Wow.
-And Mr. Rogers,

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:27.100
Pittsburgh Penguins.
Who knew?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.267
-Mr. Rogers.
Yeah, Pittsburgh.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.234
Yeah, absolutely.
-It was -- It was awesome.

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:31.667
-I mean, is this --
-I can't believe you found that.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:34.267
I mean, nothing's safe.
Nothing is safe.

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:36.167
-No, nothing's safe.
No, I have everything, yeah.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.000
Do you have one of these?
-I -- I do.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.033
I do.
-Yeah. All right, good.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:40.667
So you can keep that one.
-Okay, good.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.667
I want -- I will keep it
in mint condition.

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.767
-In mint condition, right.
I love that you put

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:45.834
the gloves on, too,
which makes me laugh.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:47.033
-Yeah, well, I --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.667
-Like, what?
For the photo shoot?

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.067
-I don't know what that was.
It had to be my choice.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:52.667
Maybe it was me
trying to be badass.

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.033
[ Laughter ]
-You're like, "I'm gonna

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.634
do something that no other
fan -- superfan will do."

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:58.300
Yeah.
-Right.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.501
-I want to congratulate you
on "Cobra Kai," by the way.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:04.033
-Thanks, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.734
Season four of "Cobra Kai" now.

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:08.868
Within days,
it became the number-one

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:10.634
most watched show globally
on Netflix.

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:11.868
-Amazing.
-Number one!

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:14.601
-Thank you!

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:18.100
-And last week, "Cobra Kai"
scored a big SAG nomination

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.300
for Outstanding
Action Performance.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.434
-Oh, the stunt --
our stunt team's amazing.

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:24.767
Amazing.
-Dude -- do you --

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:26.300
But you must get in there.
I see you.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.801
-I do get in there.
-Yeah.

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:30.133
-I do.
And we all work very, very hard.

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:34.968
We have a lot of studly, young,
amazing athletic cast members.

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:37.634
So guys like William Zabka
and myself need to --

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:38.801
need to keep up.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:39.901
And we do.
We do.

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:41.601
They --
You know, it's --

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:44.834
But, you know, I could pull,
like, my ass muscle, like,

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:47.334
with one wrong kick
without stretching.

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:49.033
It's the stretching.

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:50.167
It's all about stretching.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:51.567
-No, it is all about stretching.
Oh, my gosh.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.701
-Always about stretching.
But we --

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:56.300
You know, but what happens now,
Jimmy, is I give --

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.067
I give, like -- like, an injury
report to the stunt team.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.400
I mean, this is something
that I've done.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.567
I sort of feel like an NFL coach

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:04.901
on a Monday morning
after Sunday.

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:06.501
saying like,
"Macchio is day-to-day

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.234
with a right hamstring pull."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:09.801
-Yeah, like, "All right,
gather around, everybody."

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.334
Yeah.
-He can turn 30% to the right.

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.334
But the left side, can't let --
-Can't do it.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:16.434
-And they actually tailor
the fight scenes to my strengths

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:17.968
and make me look great,
so that's how we do it.

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:19.901
-They're like, "All right, just
use your left arm in this one."

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.133
[ Laughter ]
-That's right.

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.667
-I saw that this --
There's always surprises

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:25.601
and brand-new characters
coming in every episode.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.634
So if you haven't seen
"Cobra Kai,"

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.100
you can start season one.
You'll get it.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.901
You'll understand,
but you'll be like, "What?

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.300
Do you -- and every -- yeah.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:36.267
But this season, your actual,
real-life daughter, Julia,

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.267
is on the show with you.
-Yes, she is.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:39.467
-Not playing your daughter.
-No.

00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:40.634
-But still, there she is there.

00:05:40.634 --> 00:05:41.834
-Oh, that was us
in the dressing room.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.501
Yes, yes.
This was after we --

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:44.634
-How great is that?
-That's Julia.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:45.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:48.934
And with -- with respect
to the great Pat Morita.

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.033
-Pat Morita.
-Mr. Miyagi, you know?

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.300
-Yeah, she's wearing
a Miyagi T-shirt.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.701
I love that.
-Yeah. She --

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:54.300
She knocked it out of the park.
The writers of the show

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.400
came up with a character
for her that --

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.801
She's active, sings and dances.
And a triple threat.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:02.367
-Wow!
-And she's -- she's awesome.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.734
-Wonder where she got that from.
-Yeah, no.

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:05.601
-Yeah, exactly right.
-I'd say it skips a generation.

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:06.801
She has it.
I'm working on it.

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:09.167
-Yeah, right.
-And she --

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.200
You know, I was nervous.
You know, your own kid.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.501
-Of course.
-And listen, I went on the show,

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:14.701
but she --
they wrote her this great role,

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:17.734
and she gets to question
my parenting skills,

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:19.968
which was kind of meta
to have my own kid

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:21.834
asking me why I'm failing
as a parent.

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:23.734
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.
-It was a lot of fun.

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:25.501
-Speaking of the writing,
I should say the writing

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:27.100
is fantastic on this show.
-They are terrific.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.033
-Kudos to those writers.
-Thanks.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.634
-It's funny, it's smart,
it's interesting.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:36.200
I go -- and it's almost like
it's never-ending.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.834
I mean, this is just getting
bigger and bigger.

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.767
So it's like a -- you're
creating a whole universe.

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:42.434
-Mm-hmm. Yeah.
Listen, Jon, Josh and Hayden

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:43.634
are the main creators
of the show

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:44.934
and the entire writing staff.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:46.834
These guys,
they are truly the fans

00:06:46.834 --> 00:06:49.267
that are writing the show
for the fans.

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:51.901
So they -- they have their --

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.033
You know,
they have their big canvas

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:54.234
and all the paints up there.

00:06:54.234 --> 00:06:56.100
And they just --
It's now growing.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.901
The cast is -- is growing,
getting deeper, more --

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:02.901
The curves and turns
and twists they're taking.

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:05.834
You know, it has become --
You say that it -- it's --

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:07.734
It could go
so many different places.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:10.567
It's becoming the sort of
Karate Kid Cinematic Universe

00:07:10.567 --> 00:07:12.067
is what we talk about.
-Yeah, it is.

00:07:12.067 --> 00:07:13.300
-You know, like Marvel.
Like, I mean,

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.200
we could do prequels,
we could do movies.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.767
Maybe we'll do a spinoff
in this direction.

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:18.267
-Yeah, they can.
-I don't know where it's going.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:19.501
-It's just getting
bigger and bigger,

00:07:19.501 --> 00:07:21.167
and it's all great and all fun,
and you go --

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:23.434
-It's a lot of fun.
-And good little nods

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:25.334
to the movie.
And all the movies.

00:07:25.334 --> 00:07:26.667
-Mm-hmm.
-And it's just --

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:28.100
It's well done.
And everyone's great.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.367
Congrats on everything, buddy.
-Thank you.

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:31.634
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Ralph Macchio

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.434
and William Zabka
in "Cobra Kai."

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:34.834
Take a look at this.

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:39.033
-That's it.
Balance good.

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:41.000
Karate kick.
Everything --

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.000
-[ Grunts ]

00:07:46.067 --> 00:07:47.634
-This thing isn't even level.

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:50.534
-Or maybe you have a little
imbalance inside of you.

00:07:50.534 --> 00:07:53.167
-I still don't see me using
any of this in a real fight.

00:07:53.167 --> 00:07:56.467
-I've been trying to tell you.
Miyagi-do is not about fighting.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:07:58.634
You know what Mr. Miyagi said
was the best defense

00:07:58.634 --> 00:07:59.767
in all of karate?

00:07:59.767 --> 00:08:02.501
-High outside block
against an axe kick?

00:08:02.501 --> 00:08:06.734
-The best defense
is "no be there."

00:08:06.734 --> 00:08:08.367
-You mean, "Don't be there"?

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.834
Guy teaches you centuries
of his ancient family karate

00:08:10.834 --> 00:08:12.200
and you can't help him
with his English?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.934
-Don't even go there with me,
Johnny.

00:08:13.934 --> 00:08:15.534
-All right, are we done,
or do I have to sit in here

00:08:15.534 --> 00:08:17.901
and freeze my [bleep] off
to find inner peace?

00:08:17.901 --> 00:08:19.601
-No.
We're done.

00:08:19.601 --> 00:08:21.167
-Yeah, that's it right there.
"Yeah, we're done."

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.701
-"We're done."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:23.701 --> 00:08:26.968
-Ralph Macchio, everybody,
from the New York Islanders.

00:08:26.968 --> 00:08:28.234
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:31.801
-"Cobra Kai" season four
is streaming now on Netflix.

